From 1ea04a02f647ea2dad348d5c99d4548e47a90428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:32:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add Apple's -only-testing: and -skip-testing: options

xcodebuild selects and excludes tests with -only-testing:ID and
-skip-testing:ID, where ID is Target[/Class[/method]], and scripts
written for Apple's tools pass the same options to xctest. The runner
now accepts both. The target is the bundle's name without its
extension. -only-testing: adds to any -XCTest selection, and an
identifier naming only the target selects every test. -skip-testing:
removes tests from the selection; a skip for another target skips
nothing. As with -XCTest, a run that selects or leaves no tests fails,
and so does -only-testing: for another target, since nothing in this
bundle can match it. A malformed identifier is a usage error.

GSXCTestRunner gains -runTestsNamed:skipping:, which takes Class and
Class.method names like -runTestsNamed:; -runTestsNamed: calls it with
no skips.

This replaces PR #5, which was written against the runner before
5c84fc3.

Testing: Tests/Regression.m checks that a skip for a test that doesn't
exist changes nothing, and that skipping the selected test or its class
fails the run without running it. Tests/run.sh checks the passing and
failing combinations of the options, with -XCTest and in either order
with the bundle path, plus malformed and other-target identifiers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
